A direct remote identification add-on must broadcast the following data in real time during the entire duration of the flight, using an open and documented transmission protocol that can be received by existing mobile devices [Reg 2019/945, Part 6]:

*   **UAS operator registration number** and the verification code provided by the Member State of registration (unless the consistency check fails) [Reg 2019/945, Part 6];
*   **Unique serial number** of the add-on [Reg 2019/945, Part 6];
*   **Time stamp**, the **geographical position** of the UA, and its **height** above the surface or take-off point [Reg 2019/945, Part 6];
*   **Route course** (measured clockwise from true north) and **ground speed** of the UA [Reg 2019/945, Part 6];
*   **Geographical position** of the remote pilot or, if not available, the take-off point [Reg 2019/945, Part 6].

This information is based on the 2020 consolidated Regulation 2019/945.
